-- title:
--   Igusa bound: [±Γ_H: SL₂(ℤ)] index bounds [T:L(j)]
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $\ell\ge 3$ and $\ell\ne q$, and a positive integer $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $A$ a commutative ring with an algebra map to $L$. Assume: `hℓ`, that Katz level-$\ell$ data (points $P,Q$ on the affine Weierstrass equation with $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_\ell$ vanishing at their $x$-coordinates and the two independence elements units) transform to level-$\ell$ data under `LevelPData.variableChange`; `hM`, that the predicate `IsGamma0PowAt` (a monic kernel polynomial of degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$, or a degree-one divisor of $\Psi_2^2$ when $p^k=2$, dividing $\operatorname{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$ suitably and stable under multiplication) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A$-algebras, chord–tangent (`IsChordTangent`) and with the origin pinned (`IsOriginIdentity`); a level-$q$ Drinfeld transport datum $\mathcal T$ with `IsSectionTransport`; and the existence, in `hVC` and `hCO`, of graded ring homomorphisms realising Weierstrass variable changes and coefficient maps on the graded coordinate rings, each carrying the irrelevant ideal of the target into the image of the irrelevant ideal. Let $T$ be a field that is an $L$-algebra and an $A$-algebra compatibly, and let $x$ be a $T$-point of the moduli functor of `rigidDataPow A ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, that is, a class, modulo Weierstrass variable changes, of a Weierstrass curve over $T$ with unit discriminant together with a $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-kernel polynomial for each prime $p\mid M'$, a Katz level-$\ell$ structure, and a raw Drinfeld pair on that curve forming a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$. Suppose the $j$-invariant $j(x)\in T$ is transcendental over $L$ and $T$ is finite-dimensional over $L(j(x))$. Then the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the subgroup generated by $-1$ and by [`CohCarrier.GammaH ((q*ℓ)^2*M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) of the group $H$ of units of $\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M'$ congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$ — that is, the matrices in $\Gamma_0((q\ell)^2M')$ whose lower-right entry lies in $H$ — is at most $[T:L(j(x))]$.
--
--   This is Igusa's monodromy theorem for the elliptic curve with transcendental $j$-invariant, cast as a degree bound: a field carrying a $\Gamma_0(M')\times\Gamma(\ell)\times\Gamma(q)$-structure on such a curve must have degree over $L(j)$ at least the index of $\pm\Gamma_H$, the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ of the relevant congruence condition. It feeds the density statement for the classifying map on points with $j$-invariant the $q$-expansion parameter, used in identifying the full-level modular curve as a moduli space.
-- source:
